    { name: "Best Image to STL Converters", url: "https://image-to-stl.com/blog/best-image-to-stl-converters" }
  ]}
>
 <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Best Image to STL Converters Compared</h1>
    <p class="text-xs text-surface-400 mb-8">By Image to STL Converter Team — Updated August 8, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 mb-8">We tested the most popular free image to STL converters across three categories: browser-based, server-based, and desktop software. Here is what we found.</p>
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Browser-Based Converters (No Upload Required)</h2>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-tool border border-accent-200 dark:border-accent-800 bg-accent-50 dark:bg-accent-900/10 mb-6">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 text-sm mb-2">Image to STL Converter (image-to-stl.com) — Our Top Pick</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Why we recommend it:</strong> 100% browser-based processing means your images never leave your device. Real-time Three.js 3D preview lets you inspect the model before downloading. Three conversion modes: heightmap for reliefs, SVG extrusion for logos (unique feature among free tools), and lithophane for backlit panels. Exports to STL, OBJ, and GLB. Completely free with no registration, no limits.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Limitations:</strong> Processing quality depends on your device hardware. SVG extrusion handles common path types but very complex SVGs with hundreds of nested paths may be simplified. No batch processing for multiple images simultaneously.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed"><strong>Best for:</strong> Privacy-conscious users, anyone wanting instant results, SVG/vector enthusiasts, unlimited free conversions, beginners who want a simple workflow.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-3 mt-8">How Browser-Based Tools Compare</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Browser-based converters are the newest category of image-to-STL tools. They use JavaScript and WebGL to process images directly in your browser, avoiding the privacy and speed issues of server-based alternatives. But not all browser tools are equal — here are the key factors to evaluate:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3 mb-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">Processing Architecture</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">True browser-based tools use Canvas + WebGL APIs for local processing. Some tools claim to be "online" but actually upload your file to a server for processing — these are server-based converters with a web frontend, not genuine browser tools. You can verify by disconnecting your internet after the page loads: a true browser tool will still work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">3D Preview Quality</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">A real-time 3D preview (rotating, zooming, inspecting mesh quality) is the single most useful feature for avoiding bad prints. Without it, you are downloading blind and hoping the STL looks right in your slicer. Look for tools that let you toggle wireframe view to check mesh density and manifold status.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">Format Support</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">JPG and PNG support is universal. SVG support is rare — most tools simply rasterize SVG to pixels (losing the vector advantage). True SVG extrusion, which parses path data and extrudes into solid geometry, is a significant differentiator. OBJ and GLB export options are also uncommon in free tools.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Server-Based Converters (Upload Required)</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        These tools send your image to a remote server for processing. The advantage is that server hardware can be more powerful than your browser, enabling AI-powered depth estimation and higher polygon counts. The disadvantage is privacy, file size limits, and often daily conversion caps.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Image to STL (image-to-stl.com)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">AI-powered server-side conversion. Uses machine learning to estimate depth from single photos, producing more natural-looking reliefs than simple brightness-based heightmaps. Supports multiple output formats (STL, OBJ, GLB, FBX). The free tier limits you to a few conversions per day, and your images are uploaded to their servers. Quality is good for complex photos but the privacy tradeoff is significant.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">AnyConv / Convertio</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">General-purpose file converters that happen to support image-to-STL among hundreds of other format pairs. The STL conversion is basic heightmap-only with no 3D preview, no SVG support, and no parameter tuning. Useful for one-off conversions if you already use these platforms, but not suitable for anyone who needs quality control over their 3D models. Free tiers are limited by file count or file size.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Selva3D</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Dedicated image-to-3D service with a simple interface. Upload a photo and get a heightmap-based STL. The free tier produces low-resolution output with a watermark — full resolution requires a paid plan. No SVG support, no lithophane mode, and no OBJ/GLB export. Decent for testing the concept but not suitable for regular use without paying.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-900/10">
        <h4 class="font-medium text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 text-xs mb-1">When to Choose Server-Based</h4>
        <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Server-based tools make sense when you need AI-powered depth estimation from a single photo (which browsers cannot do well yet), or when you are converting very large batches where server processing speed outweighs upload time. For most users, the privacy, speed, and unlimited nature of browser tools is the better choice.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Desktop Software</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Desktop programs offer the most control and the highest output quality, but require software installation and a learning curve. They are the right choice when you need complete creative control.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Blender (Free)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Full 3D creation suite used by professionals. The Displace modifier can convert images to 3D reliefs with full control over every parameter. Supports sculpting, mesh repair, and multi-material export. The downside: significant learning curve. Expect 10-20 hours to become comfortable enough to produce quality image-to-3D conversions. If you are willing to invest the time, Blender produces the best results of any tool in this comparison.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Cura (Free)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Ultimaker Cura is primarily a 3D printer slicer, but it has a lesser-known ability to import JPG/PNG images and convert them to lithophanes directly. The workflow is simple: drag an image into Cura, set the dimensions, and it generates a printable lithophane STL. Limited to lithophane-style output only — no heightmap reliefs or SVG extrusion. Excellent for quick lithophanes if you already use Cura.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Fusion 360 / SolidWorks</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Professional CAD software primarily for engineering and mechanical design, not artistic image conversion. You can import an image as a canvas, trace it manually, and extrude into 3D, but there is no automatic image-to-STL pipeline. Suitable only if you need precise, dimensioned models derived from reference images and already have CAD experience.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">How to Choose: A Decision Framework</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">The right tool depends on what you are making and your priorities:</p>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">If privacy matters most</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Use a browser-based tool. Verify by disconnecting your internet after the page loads — the converter should still work. Our tool is designed explicitly for this use case.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">If you want the highest possible quality</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Learn Blender. No browser or server tool matches the control you get from a full 3D suite, especially for sculpting, mesh repair, and multi-material workflows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">If you need batch processing</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Server-based tools can process multiple images in parallel on cloud hardware. Browser tools process one at a time (sequentially on your device). For occasional use, browser tools are fine. For 50+ images regularly, a server tool or Blender script may be worth the tradeoffs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-tool border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 text-xs mb-1">If you are converting logos or vector art</h4>
          <p class="text-2xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Use a tool with SVG extrusion support. Raster-based conversion of logos produces pixelated edges that look poor when 3D printed. True vector extrusion preserves sharp edges and clean geometry.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Comparison Table</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-700"><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Feature</th><th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 bg-accent-50 dark:bg-accent-900/10">Our Tool</th><th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-medium">Server AI</th><th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-medium">Blender</th><th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-medium">Cura</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-surface-100 dark:divide-surface-800"><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Privacy (no uploads)</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">Yes</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">No</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Yes</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Yes</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">3D Preview</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">Real-time</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Limited</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Native</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Slice preview</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">SVG Extrusion</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">Yes (unique)</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">No</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Manual</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">No</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">AI Depth Estimation</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">No</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium">Yes</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Plugins</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">No</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Free Tier</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">Unlimited</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Limited</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Free (OSS)</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Free</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Learning Curve</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">None</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">None</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Steep</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">Low</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Export Formats</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center text-accent-600 font-medium bg-accent-50/50">STL/OBJ/GLB</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">STL/OBJ/FBX</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">All formats</td><td class="py-2 px-2 text-center">STL only</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
+      <p class="text-2xs text-surface-400 mt-2">Comparison based on testing conducted August 2026. Features and pricing may change.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-tool border border-accent-200 dark:border-accent-800 bg-accent-50 dark:bg-accent-900/10 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 mb-3">Our pick: the only free, private, browser-based image to STL converter with real-time 3D preview and SVG support. Try it now — no registration, no uploads, no limits.</p>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-accent-600 hover:bg-accent-700 text-white text-sm font-medium transition-colors">Start Converting Free</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
